<title>BELGIUM: EC, Bonn set more talks on car tax plans.</title>
<headline>EC, Bonn set more talks on car tax plans.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission and German government representatives plan to hold further talks on Bonn's plans to reduce taxes for low-emission automobiles.</p>
<p>At a meeting on Friday, the two sides shared the goals of encouraging the auto industry to produce more low-emission vehicles, and are now seeking the proper legal solution, a commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>The commission thinks Bonn's draft legislation, which would eliminate taxes for cars that meet the strictest emission standards, goes beyond established European norms and would impair competition.</p>
</text>
